WEBVTT

00:13:59.875 --> 00:14:02.643
Being a steamroller
was putting his future in jeopardy.

00:14:02.667 --> 00:14:05.268
JB: Maybe I had some success
with it at the start,

00:14:05.292 --> 00:14:08.601
but I also learned
that for long-term relationships,

00:14:08.625 --> 00:14:12.309
it wasn't gonna be a recipe for success.

00:14:12.333 --> 00:14:16.226
AG: With his steamrolling style,
Jason was looking out for himself,

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.559
but it turns out
there's actually a lot of value

00:14:18.583 --> 00:14:20.809
for both relationships and results

00:14:20.833 --> 00:14:23.434
in helping the other party benefit.

00:14:23.458 --> 00:14:25.726
In one of my favorite studies,
researchers found

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:28.434
that the more intelligent
negotiators were,

00:14:28.458 --> 00:14:30.250
the better their counterparts did.